% G2 Propeller control and overspeed protection (design decisions, delegated by Hamit):
% single-acting propeller that feathers on counterweights and springs when the pitch-oil pressure is lost (A-04,
% PC-12 class; PIF-03 closed); in-flight low-pitch stop that no single failure can remove (14 CFR 35.21(a)); FADEC
% feather command through a feather solenoid on the PCU that dumps the PCU output, independent of the PCU governor
% and the OSG. The PCU has its own governor pump on its drive (pad 1.81 N m at 1,699 rpm, about 320 W, servo about
% 2.6 MPa), its inlet fed from the RGB supply (ICD-12). Governor drives stay on the PT side (a propeller-side
% PCU / OSG drive was considered and not taken: 3.9 mass and layout).
% Speed signals: protection Np from the core's PT-rotor wheel upstream of the PT-end coupling (ICD-36, core maker);
% control Np on the input pinion F203 (C-05), also a cross-check; Nr on P103 between the carrier front plate
% (z 117) and the front NU1024 (z 413), at z 400 (TBR, 3.9 CAD). Logic: 3% mismatch (step 1.4), absolute Np trip
% at abs_trip with a confirming cue; signal validation inhibits the comparison on a lost or implausible signal.
% Breaks: FMEA ids, text, the PT-side DOFs of the step 2.3 model in rigid rotation (the first n_up of PT,
% couplings, pinion, gear 2 with the generator branch, sun, planets, carrier), added inertia [kg m2], logic.
br = @(fm, en, tr, zone, n_up, logic) struct('fm', fm, 'en', en, 'tr', tr, 'zone', zone, 'n_up', n_up, 'J_add', 0, ...
                                            'logic', logic);
in.prot = struct('Q0', 417.3, 'n0', 22000, 'mismatch', 0.03, 'abs_trip', 1.06, 't_end', 8, 'z_Nr', 400);
