% D1b Dual failures (sf_fta2). Rates per hour; checked elements: lam (latent, found at the check), T (check
% interval) [h], qd (failure on demand); all TBR (engineering assumptions until supplier data).
% (a) PT overspeed: the drive-chain breaks the G2 coverage table protects (rate basis of D1: 1e-6 per hour for a
% non-critical structural element, 1e-7 for a CS-E 515 critical part); the protection speed signals: n_ch pairs (two
% independent protection Np probes on the core PT rotor, ICD-36, and the two Nr pickups) with 1-out-of-2 trip logic
% (either valid channel trips with the G2 confirming cue; cross-channel validation and the pinion-Np comparison): a
% pair is lost when both probes are lost, independently ((1 - beta) lambda T)^2 / 3, or by a common cause
% beta lambda T / 2, with beta 0.05 (IEC 61508-6 Annex D, sensors with separate harnesses and connectors, TBR);
% n_probe probes for the spurious trips (any one with a false confirming cue trips); the fuel shut-off valve and the logic, the whole channel
% checked at each start (14 CFR 33.28(f)(2): T one A-05 mission); spurious trips: a pickup fault with a false
% confirming cue, against an aircraft-side allowance (STANAG 4671 class to be confirmed, TBR)
in.ft2.a = struct('n_ch', 2, 'beta', 0.05, 'n_probe', 4, 'ch', struct('lam', 1e-5, 'T', in.mission_h, 'qd', 0), ...
    'valve', struct('lam', 2e-6, 'T', in.mission_h, 'qd', 5e-5), 'logic', struct('lam', 1e-6, 'T', in.mission_h, 'qd', 1e-6), ...
    'p_false', 0.01, 'spur_allow', 1e-6);
in.ft2.a.rows = {'FM01 input pinion teeth', 1e-6; 'FM04 gear 2 teeth', 1e-6; 'FM05 gear 2 web (FM08 through it)', 1e-6; ...
    'FM09 sun teeth', 1e-6; 'FM13 ring seat and lugs', 1e-6; 'FM18 sun quill and splines', 1e-6; ...
    'FM31 intermediate shaft (downstream part)', 1e-6; 'FM17 carrier (P103, critical)', 1e-7; ...
    'FM19 P103 outboard of the QJ1024 (critical)', 1e-7; 'FM21 P103 inboard of the QJ1024 (critical)', 1e-7; ...
    'FM28 RGB input shaft (critical)', 1e-7; 'FM29 PT output shaft (critical)', 1e-7; ...
    'FM30 diaphragm coupling, PT end (critical)', 1e-7; 'FM30 diaphragm coupling, RGB end (critical)', 1e-7};
% (b) hazardous propeller effect: initiators and layers
in.ft2.b = struct('fine', struct('lam', 1e-5), 'cross', struct('lam', 1e-6), 'block', struct('lam', 1e-6), ...
    'ifsd', struct('lam', 1e-5, 'T', in.mission_h), ...
    'osg', struct('lam', 5e-6, 'lam_drive', 1e-6, 'T', in.tbo_h, 'qd', 1e-4), ...
    'lps', struct('lam', 1e-6, 'T', in.tbo_h, 'qd', 1e-4), 'ff', struct('lam', 1e-5, 'T', in.mission_h, 'qd', 1e-4), ...
    'cw', struct('lam', 1e-6, 'T', in.mission_h, 'qd', 1e-4));
% fine: PCU fail-to-fine with its drive and pump intact; cross: lube-to-pitch cross-leak at L403; block: L403 / L404
% blockage; ifsd: an in-flight shutdown later in the mission (exposure half a mission); osg: OSG internal and drive
% (FM56) latent rates, test with the test solenoid at T (TBO to start); lps: in-flight low-pitch stop (checked at T);
% ff: FADEC feather command and feather solenoid (tested at each start); cw: counterweight feathering (exercised at
% each shutdown)
in.ft2.b.down = {'FM09 sun teeth', 1e-6; 'FM13 ring seat and lugs', 1e-6; 'FM17 carrier (critical)', 1e-7; ...
    'FM18 sun quill and splines', 1e-6; 'FM21 P103 inboard (critical)', 1e-7; 'FM31 intermediate shaft (downstream part)', 1e-6};
in.ft2.b.cc = {'FM05 gear 2 web', 1e-6; 'FM63 F204 stub between gear 2 and the PCU and pump drives', 1e-6};
% one-at-a-time x10 sensitivity: field paths (a cell list of rates is scaled as a whole)
in.ft2.sens = {{'a', 'rows'}, {'a', 'ch', 'lam'}, {'a', 'valve', 'lam'}, {'a', 'valve', 'qd'}, {'a', 'logic', 'lam'}, ...
               {'a', 'logic', 'qd'}, {'b', 'fine', 'lam'}, {'b', 'cross', 'lam'}, {'b', 'osg', 'lam'}, {'b', 'osg', 'lam_drive'}, ...
               {'b', 'osg', 'qd'}, {'b', 'cc'}, {'b', 'down'}, {'b', 'lps', 'lam'}, {'b', 'ff', 'lam'}, {'b', 'cw', 'lam'}, ...
               {'b', 'cw', 'qd'}};

% D5 Fire (SAF-05, CS-E 130, 14 CFR 33.17): standard flame of ISO 2685 (1100 +- 80 degC, 116 +- 10 kW/m2 on the cold
% calorimeter); durations from CS-Definitions (EASA) and AC 33.17-1B (FAA, 20 May 2025, with AC 20-135A recognising
% SAE AS6826; a test on the FAA route uses the AS6826 flame, not the ISO 2685 flame used here).
% F1 decisions (delegated by Hamit; batch 3):
% 1. Zone: the first-stage side of the RGB (F201 with its rear wall, accessory cover, A304, pump pack, filter,
%    manifold, valves, PCU, OSG, tubes, hoses) is in the designated fire zone (the accessory section, about 330 mm
%    from the 650-700 degC exhaust collector, ICD-18); tank C-15 and the cooler are aircraft items in or next to it.
% 2. Mount structure and retention path (CS-E 130(g)): P101 (shell, nose, mount flange ring, pads), the propeller
%    shaft and the retention path are outside the zone by the installation partition declared under CS-E 30 (a
%    firewall with a fire seal at the P101 / F201 joint plane, ICD-39); the P101 flange is heated only by conduction
%    across the joint. Fallback (option considered, not taken): an engine fire shield over the flange ring, pads and
%    nose, about 0.6 kg TBR, which would take SYS-06 past 110 kg.
% 3. Aircraft items: ICD-39 to ICD-44 (partition, detection and extinguishing, fuel shut-off, tank, cooler and hoses,
%    automatic shutdown and feather).
% 4. Level of the oil parts in the zone: the RGB has no oil shut-off valve, but the shutdown and feather stop the
%    propeller, the PT and all pumps (counterweight feathering, G2); the time to zero flow is t_zero below (about
%    48 s), under 5 min, so the oil-carrying parts are rated fire resistant (5 min at the minimum representative
%    flow) on both routes (CS-E 130 with AMC E 130; 14 CFR 33.17 with AC 33.17-1B 6.3.2); the tank stays fireproof
%    (ICD-42). Oil left in the RGB parts after the flow stops: the hold-up V_hold (TBR) and the tank.
in.fire_zone = struct('t_detect', 10, 't_logic', 2, 't_feather', 6, 't_rundown', 30, 'V_hold', 0.5, 'V_tank', 5.69);
% s, s, s, s (TBR: ICD-40, ICD-44, G2 counterweights, run-down of the feathered propeller and PT until the pump
% delivery is below its minimum), L (oil left in the case, cover and pump pack after the drain, TBR), L (ICD-42)
in.fire = struct('T_f', 1100 + 80, 'q0', 116e3 + 10e3, 'T0', 20, 'k', 152, 'rho', 2680, 'cp', @(T) 920 + 0.45 * T, ...
    'T_sink', 149 + 21, 'T_solidus', 555, 'h_noflow', 10, 't_flow', 300, 't_after', 600);
% Flame at its upper tolerance (ISO 2685 1100 + 80 degC, 116 + 10 kW/m2), the basis of every result. k, rho, cp(T):
% A357-T6 (cp 963 J/kgK at 20 degC rising about 0.45 J/kgK per K, TBR). T_sink: the highest in-service scavenge oil
% temperature, the LUB-02 149 degC inlet limit plus the 21 K scavenge rise of the 3.2 / 2.7 heat balance (AC 33.17-1B
% 8.3.1); the wall starts there. T_solidus: incipient melting of A357.0, about 555 degC (TBR). h_noflow: oil side after
% the flow stops (residual film and air, bound). t_flow: 5 min with oil flow (fire resistant); t_after: the zero-flow
% phase after it, restarted from the end-of-flow profile (10 min, the fireproof extension, reported only)
in.fire.sy_T = [20 240; 100 230; 150 215; 200 185; 250 140; 300 80; 350 45; 400 30; 450 20; 500 12; 555 0];
% short-time hot yield of A357-T6 after a brief exposure [degC, MPa], typical Al-Si-Mg T6 casting values. No MMPDS /
% MIL-HDBK-5J table for A357-T6 / T61 at 1/2 h exposure was available here: an uncertainty listed in SAF-05 (TBR); a
% 1/2 h table is conservative for a 5 min exposure (the time-dependent allowable)
in.fire.E = 72e3;  in.fire.alpha = 21.5e-6;   % MPa, 1/K: thermal stress of a locally heated zone E alpha dT / 2 (secondary)
in.fire.oil = struct('rho', 880, 'nu', 2.2e-6, 'k', 0.13, 'cp', 2300, 'flash', 270, 'ait', 404, 'L_fp', 0.1);
% oil at 170 degC (MIL-PRF-23699 class, Mobil Jet Oil II data sheet: flash about 270 degC, auto-ignition about 404 degC;
% rho, nu, k, cp TBR); L_fp: flame footprint along the film [m] for the film energy balance
in.fire.Q_rgb = 20.1;                        % L/min into the RGB sump at MC (3.2 network, pump delivery 30.5 L/min)
in.fire.n_min = 0.60;                        % the lowest flow: ground and flight idle at 60% PT speed (3.2 in.ops; the
                                             % pump delivery scales with speed, TBR): 12.1 L/min
% Oil-side h of a laminar drain film (Nusselt film on the bore): delta = (3 nu Gamma / (rho g))^(1/3) with Gamma the
% mass flow per unit width round the bore, h = 1.88 k / delta (thermally developed, uniform flux, free surface); the
% jets themselves are not credited. Walls (s_req: the operating stress of the wall from 3.5 / 3.6: planetary case
% 16.7 + 12.2 MPa planet pass; first-stage case 28.7 MPa steady bound (a limit-load peak, conservative) + 9.35 MPa
% vibratory; no p r / t: the case is vented). zone: in the designated fire zone (true) or behind the partition
% (fallback case only)
in.fire.walls = struct( ...
    'name', {'F201 side wall (drain film)', 'F201 upper wall and bosses (no film)', ...
             'P101 shell, drain film (fallback: no partition)', 'P101 shell under the ring-gear seat (fallback)'}, ...
    'name_tr', {'F201 yan duvarı (boşaltma filmi)', 'F201 üst duvarı ve göbekleri (film yok)', ...
                'P101 kabuğu, boşaltma filmi (yedek durum: bölme yok)', 'P101 kabuğu, çember dişli yuvası altı (yedek durum)'}, ...
    't', {6, 6, 8, 8}, 'ri', {129.5, 129.5, 129.5, 129.5}, 'share', {0.5, 0, 0.5, 0}, 'h_fixed', {NaN, 20, NaN, 75}, ...
    's_req', {28.7 + 9.35, 28.7 + 9.35, 16.7 + 12.2, 16.7 + 12.2}, 'zone', {true, true, false, false});
% share: the part of the RGB flow that drains as a film over the wall (TBR, the split of the jets between the stages);
% h_fixed: no film: upper walls, bosses and pads 0-20 W/m2K (20 used); the shell bore under the 70 mm ring-gear seat
% (about 59% of the bore length) where the A357 grows away from the steel ring in the fire (gap about 0.3-0.7 mm): air
% 75-150 W/m2K (75 used), trapped oil 220-430 W/m2K
% The P101 / F201 joint (F3, sf_fire_joint): oil-side h of the F201 film (560 W/m2K, the F2 basis), explicit step [s].
% Joint items: C-03 O-rings AMS 7287 fluorocarbon rated about 204 degC; C-02 secondary seals unspecified; 30 x M6 12.9
% from the P101 side into helical coil inserts in F201: seat pressure on A357 about 230 MPa (218-242) on the 10 / 6.6
% mm seat (44.3 mm2), preload F_M = p A; insert thread stress about 101 MPa at F_M; thermal preload about +6 kN per bolt
% at 360 degC (the steel bolt against the A357 grip); operating joint load per bolt F_A about 0.7 kN (first-stage gear
% forces at MC, 12.1 / 4.6 / 3.2 kN, on a 0.1 m arm to the joint plane over 30 bolts on PCD 308; TBR), load factor
% Phi 0.1; 3.9 option: a steel load-spreading washer of 16 mm outside diameter (167 mm2)
in.fire.joint = struct('h', 560, 'dt', 0.01, 'T_oring', 204, 'p_seat', 230, 'A_seat', pi / 4 * (10^2 - 6.6^2), ...
    's_ins', 101, 'dF_th', 6e3, 'F_A', 700, 'Phi', 0.1, 'A_washer', pi / 4 * (16^2 - 6.6^2));

